    <GaugingStation location="Tir-y-dail" name="Loughor" number="59002">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station with bed control (crude oblique Crump weir) built over sewer crossing. Flow affected by PWS abstraction and effluent returns.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Rb overtopped on rare occasions. One peak flow rating applied across period of record. Bankfull is thought to be somewhere between 2.0 and 2.2m. For now the upper limit is 2.2m but this will be revised by site survey.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station with bed control (crude oblique Crump weir) built over sewer crossing.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">PWS abstraction from main spring source. GW and industrial abstractions and effluent returns.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Southern half of catchment is mainly Coal Measures; Millstone Grit, Carboniferous Limestone and Old Red Sandstone in northern half. Extensive Boulder Clay cover at lower elevations. Mainly dairy farming and some patches of forest.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">PGEI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Good confidence in rating at QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Few high flow gaugings. Rating cannot be validated beyond QMED." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
